# Copy this file to ".env" and fill it in. NEVER commit your real .env.
#
# --- Authentication (required) ---
#
# This tool signs in ONLY as a read-only app registration that you create. It never
# signs in as a person, never opens a login prompt, and never shows a device code.
# Fill in all three. The app's own token covers every plane - Graph, Azure, Dataverse,
# Power Platform. The exact least-privilege permissions are in docs/permissions.md,
# and every run starts with a setup check that tells you what is missing and how to
# fix it (run it alone with: pwsh ./scripts/check-setup.ps1).
TENANT_ID=
CLIENT_ID=
CLIENT_SECRET=
#
# --- Scope ---
#
# Dataverse environments to audit (comma-separated URLs). Leave blank to auto-discover
# them from the Power Platform sweep; the basic dataverse-sweep runs only for URLs listed here.
DATAVERSE_ENVIRONMENTS=
#
# Azure subscriptions to audit (comma-separated IDs). Leave blank to audit every
# subscription the app can read (the app needs the Reader role - see docs/permissions.md).
AZURE_SUBSCRIPTIONS=
#
# --- Optional AI analysis of the findings (OFF by default) ---
#
# Adds a mitigation-analysis section. Two honest notes: the default is off, so the
# "nothing leaves your tenant" posture is unchanged unless you turn this on; and 'api' mode
# SENDS the scoped findings to the endpoint you configure - the one thing this tool can send
# off-machine, and only when you set it.
#
# Mode: off | local | api
#   off   - do nothing (default).
#   local - write output/ai-analysis-prompt.md (findings + a ready prompt) to hand to your own
#           Claude Code / Kimi / Codex session. No network call, zero egress.
#   api   - call the OpenAI-compatible endpoint below and write output/ai-analysis.md.
AI_ANALYSIS=off
#
# What the analysis may see: redacted (names/UPNs/emails/IPs/GUIDs masked - recommended) |
# named (real names kept) | full (summaries plus raw evidence files; most exposure).
AI_ANALYSIS_SCOPE=redacted
#
# For AI_ANALYSIS=api only. Any OpenAI-compatible chat/completions endpoint + key + model.
# Works with OpenAI, Azure OpenAI (in your own tenant), Anthropic's compat endpoint, Moonshot/Kimi, etc.
#   OpenAI:     AI_API_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions      AI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
#   Anthropic:  AI_API_URL=https://api.anthropic.com/v1/chat/completions   AI_MODEL=claude-opus-5
#   Kimi:       AI_API_URL=https://api.moonshot.ai/v1/chat/completions     AI_MODEL=kimi-k2-0905-preview
AI_API_URL=
AI_API_KEY=
AI_MODEL=
